OL,3,GNEWSADry summer puts horse racing
OL,4,Aseason under threat
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe dry summer risks disrupting the
OL,7,Fearly months of the horse racing jumps
OL,8,Fseason, with racecourses warning
OL,9,Ffixtures could be cancelled unless
OL,10,Fsignificant rain arrives in the coming
OL,11,Fweeks.
OL,13,FTom Ryall, clerk of the course at
OL,14,FWincanton Racecourse in Somerset, said
OL,15,F"a constant wet period for the next two
OL,16,Fmonths" is needed to make the ground
OL,17,Fsoft enough to race on for their first
OL,18,Ffixture of the season on 25 October.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
